BRIEF: session 23, a walk down whole repository trees guided by folder summaries, pre-registered while the session 19 pod is embedding

Whole repositories of session 19's pool (seed 20261106; at least 8 directories with a kept file, depth 2, 40 to 300 kept files, 5 images and 5 others; 200 trees or 22,000 files). Every directory has a summary of its own files and one of its subtree; a greedy reader walks from the root to the query's directory. Three tests under E1 at 2 KiB: the per-kind sample that merges against the mean on minority queries (H23a), against the uniform sample (H23b), and the walk against reading every directory (H23c); names and chance beside them. scripts/tree_fetch.py, scripts/tree.py, scripts/s23_selftest.py (a second, plain implementation: 32,945 values agree on synthetic trees), scripts/s23_run.sh, and the call at the end of scripts/s19_followup.sh (the session 21 part of that script is unchanged). Read before the commit by a reviewer instance that had not seen the code; its findings are listed in the brief. No retrieval number of the new source exists yet.

